A41 — bound the composite constants UBO range

The composite binds its push constants as a uniform buffer: the upload buffer at
the offset uploadConstants staged them, with range VK_WHOLE_SIZE. That makes the
descriptor's range the rest of the upload buffer — megabytes — which is past
maxUniformBufferRange (64 KiB on Turnip and Mali) and so invalid usage.

It went unnoticed while the buffer was 1920x1080x4 bytes. Since A39 the buffer
is the output frame rounded up to whole MiB, which on a 1920x1080 output is
exactly 8 MiB. Turnip stores a UBO's size in vec4s in a 15-bit field, so with
the constants at offset 0 an 8 MiB range (0x80000 vec4s) wraps to zero, the
shader reads all-zero constants, and every composited frame comes out black.
Direct scanout never touches the UBO, which is why the picture only goes black
once something forces the composite: a colour look (A31) or a ReShade effect.

Bind at most maxUniformBufferRange from the constants' offset, read once from
the device properties.

The accessor and the member are declared past the lines A39 adds (after
supportsModifiers() and after m_submissionSeqNo) rather than next to the upload
buffer declarations. Placing them in A39's own context makes this patch and A39
each fail the other's reverse test, and then neither can be recognised as
already applied and the train stops re-applying.

--- a/src/rendervulkan.cpp
+++ b/src/rendervulkan.cpp
@@ -428,6 +428,7 @@
 	VkPhysicalDeviceProperties props;
 	vk.GetPhysicalDeviceProperties( m_physDev, &props );
 	vk_log.infof( "selecting physical device '%s': queue family %x (general queue family %x)", props.deviceName, m_queueFamily, m_generalQueueFamily );
+	m_uMaxUniformBufferRange = props.limits.maxUniformBufferRange;
 
 	return true;
 }
@@ -1851,7 +1852,12 @@
 
 	scratchDescriptor.buffer = m_device->m_uploadBuffer;
 	scratchDescriptor.offset = m_renderBufferOffset;
-	scratchDescriptor.range = VK_WHOLE_SIZE;
+	// The constants live in the upload buffer, which is output-sized since A39
+	// (8 MiB on 1080p). VK_WHOLE_SIZE makes the range the rest of that buffer,
+	// past maxUniformBufferRange — invalid usage, and Turnip then wraps the
+	// UBO's 15-bit vec4 size field to zero, so the shader reads all-zero
+	// constants and every composited frame is black.
+	scratchDescriptor.range = std::min<VkDeviceSize>( m_device->upload_buffer_size - m_renderBufferOffset, m_device->maxUniformBufferRange() );
 
 	for (uint32_t i = 0; i < VKR_SAMPLER_SLOTS; i++)
 	{
--- a/src/rendervulkan.hpp
+++ b/src/rendervulkan.hpp
@@ -871,6 +871,7 @@
 	inline VkPipelineLayout pipelineLayout() {return m_pipelineLayout;}
 	inline int drmRenderFd() {return m_drmRendererFd;}
 	inline bool supportsModifiers() {return m_bSupportsModifiers;}
+	inline uint32_t maxUniformBufferRange() {return m_uMaxUniformBufferRange;}
 	inline bool hasDrmPrimaryDevId() {return m_bHasDrmPrimaryDevId;}
 	inline dev_t primaryDevId() {return m_drmPrimaryDevId;}
 	inline bool supportsFp16() {return m_bSupportsFp16;}
@@ -971,6 +972,7 @@
 
 	VkSemaphore m_scratchTimelineSemaphore;
 	std::atomic<uint64_t> m_submissionSeqNo = { 0 };
+	uint32_t m_uMaxUniformBufferRange = 16384;
 	std::vector<std::unique_ptr<CVulkanCmdBuffer>> m_unusedCmdBufs;
 	std::map<uint64_t, std::unique_ptr<CVulkanCmdBuffer>> m_pendingCmdBufs;
 
